# CrossRef Local Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and customize as needed

# =============================================================================
# LOCAL MODE - Direct store access
# =============================================================================
#
# There is no database-path variable. The corpus lives in the fleet's shared
# store primitive, and the connection is resolved by
# scitex_dev.store.host_store(), which honours SCITEX_STORE_DSN and otherwise
# reaches this host's own store. That resolver is the single source of truth;
# this package neither reads a DSN itself nor keeps a second copy of one.
#
# Set SCITEX_STORE_DSN only to point at a store other than this host's.
#
# NEVER commit a real DSN — it can carry a password. Keep it in your own .env
# (which is gitignored), your shell profile, or a mode-0600 environment file.
#
# SCITEX_STORE_DSN=<connection string for the shared store>

# =============================================================================
# DEVELOPMENT / DEBUGGING
# =============================================================================

# Enable debug mode for verbose logging
# CROSSREF_LOCAL_DEBUG_MODE=1

# Cache directory (default: ~/.cache/crossref-local)
# CROSSREF_LOCAL_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache

# Offline ingest feed: when set to a JSON file of CrossRef `message` pages,
# `crossref-local update-db` reads from it instead of the network.
# CROSSREF_LOCAL_UPDATE_FEED=/path/to/feed.json

# =============================================================================
# REMOTE MODE - HTTP API access (via SSH tunnel or direct connection)
# =============================================================================

# Force remote mode (set to "remote" or "local")
# CROSSREF_LOCAL_MODE=remote

# API URL for remote mode (default: http://localhost:31291)
# CROSSREF_LOCAL_API_URL=http://localhost:31291

# Server host/port (for run-server-http)
# CROSSREF_LOCAL_HOST=0.0.0.0
# CROSSREF_LOCAL_PORT=31291

# =============================================================================
# SCITEX INTEGRATION (takes priority over CROSSREF_LOCAL_* variables)
# =============================================================================
# Port scheme: 3129X (31290: scitex-cloud, 31291: crossref, 31292: openalex)
#
# SCITEX_SCHOLAR_CROSSREF_MODE=remote
# SCITEX_SCHOLAR_CROSSREF_HOST=0.0.0.0
# SCITEX_SCHOLAR_CROSSREF_PORT=31291

# =============================================================================
# TYPICAL SSH TUNNEL SETUP
# =============================================================================
# 1. Create SSH tunnel to the host running the HTTP API:
#    ssh -L 31291:127.0.0.1:31291 your-api-host
#
# 2. Set environment variables:
#    export CROSSREF_LOCAL_MODE=remote
#    export CROSSREF_LOCAL_API_URL=http://localhost:31291
#
# 3. Or use CLI flags:
#    crossref-local --http search "machine learning"
#    crossref-local --api-url http://localhost:31291 search "query"
